# @see docs/audits/ai-slop-audit.md F-004
id: SLOP-118
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 3
action: advisory
title: Non-portable sed -i usage
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .cpp .c .h .sh .bash
  exclude_paths: vendor/ node_modules/ .git/
  content_contains: sed
patterns:
  - regex: sed\s+-i\s+''
    message: "macOS-only sed — GNU/Linux sed requires 'sed -i' without empty string argument"
  - regex: sed\s+-i\s+""
    message: "macOS-only sed — GNU/Linux sed requires 'sed -i' without empty string argument"
  - regex: sed\s+-i\s+'s/
    message: "macOS-only sed — this form works on GNU but fails on BSD/macOS (needs -i '')"
fix: "Use a portable alternative: read file → modify in memory → write to tmpfile → rename (or use perl -pi -e which is portable)"
